{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_001 demands a causal mechanism for independence but offers only a counting proxy (evidence-ref overlap). The problem explicitly asks what evidence distinguishes genuine independent verification from mere restatement, and where a claim can be tested by counting or execution, say exactly what to count/execute. SRC_001 proposes counting citation-set overlap, but provides no causal story for WHY low overlap entails independent verification: two engines can cite disjoint evidence blocks yet still rest on the same latent shortcut/bias (restatement via different citations), or cite high-overlap blocks yet re-derive independently. The mechanism never identifies the distinguishing observable — it assumes correlation between lexical divergence and causal independence without justifying the link the problem asks it to establish.","counterexample":["Author cites block A and concludes X.","Checker cites disjoint block B and concludes X, but both blocks A and B were co-generated from the same upstream latent failure.","Evidence-ref intersection is empty (maximally 'divergent' by SRC_001's count), yet verification is not independent."],"target_alias":"SRC_001"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_002 asserts a 'contradiction' relation to the traditional separate-weights requirement and a 'shared mechanism' with SRC_001, but the asserted contradiction is not substantiated: the problem context for 091742a8f728 describes binding the conjecture role group to the second model in a two-engine split; it says nothing that contradicts requiring different model weights — a two-engine run can still have separate weights. The target labels this as 'contradicts ... by sharing a mechanism with SRC_001' without identifying a causal/mechanistic incompatibility, so the relation is a misnamed summary, not a substantive dependence/reduction/contradiction. The relation-form commitment is mechanically satisfied, but the substance fails the neighbourhood-connection standard.","counterexample":["A run uses engine A (coder group) and engine B (conjecture group) with different training histories AND separate weights; the 091742a8f728 context is satisfied and the separate-weights requirement is also satisfied — no contradiction arises.","Thus 'contradicts the traditional requirement for separate model weights' is false as stated."],"target_alias":"SRC_002"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_03 asserts 'Separation is necessary because single-engine verification is fundamentally a measure of self-consistency,' but its own countercondition concedes a case where single-engine verification can shift the truth-source to symbolic execution. By admitting an executable-sandbox countercondition under 'observation,' the target's necessity claim is no longer unconditional — it acknowledges a mechanism by which the same engine can obtain an external truth-source rather than merely self-consistency. Yet the claim and mechanism still assert unconditional necessity (perfect correlation of error terms) without reconciling how the conceded execution-based pathway leaves self-consistency as the only thing measured.","counterexample":["The target's own countercondition: 'The verification process involves executing code in an external sandbox, shifting the truth-source from latent weights to symbolic execution.' Under this admitted case, a single engine can verify via execution, so separation is not necessary in the way the claim asserts."],"target_alias":"SRC_003"}]}